<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Esau de' Buondelmonti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1411">1411</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Esau de' Buondelmonti was a Florentine nobleman who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ioannina">Ioannina</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> from 1385 to 1411. He married Maria Angelina Doukaina Palaiologina, widow of the murdered ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-preljubovic">Thomas Preljubović</a>, and governed with Byzantine support. In 1399 he was captured in battle by the Albanian lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjon-zenebishi">Gjon Zenebishi</a> and later ransomed. After his death his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlo-i-tocco">Carlo I Tocco</a> took Ioannina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/esau-de-buondelmonti.jpg" alt="Esau de' Buondelmonti" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Constantine Plakidas · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_Esau_de%27_Buondelmonti.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
